#metadata((
  title: "Building a reading routine",
  description: "A small system for making technical reading part of ordinary work.",
  date: "2022-07-08",
  image: "/assets/cover-first.jpg",
)) <aster-frontmatter>

Reading becomes easier to sustain when it has a regular place in the week. Keep
the queue short, choose one question before opening a document, and stop when
you can explain one useful idea in your own words.

Notes do not need to become polished essays. A sentence about what changed in
your understanding is often enough to make the next reading session productive.

= Keep the loop small

Pick one source, record one idea, and connect it to one current task. A compact
loop is more valuable than an elaborate archive that is difficult to revisit.
